# Cline Workspace Rules — NTPE AI Workspace v2.0

## Project
NTPE (Novel Translation Pipeline Engine) — Python-based literary translation pipeline with multi-provider AI orchestration, quality engine, and enterprise deployment framework.

## Language
- Primary: Python (3.x)
- Documentation: Markdown
- Configuration: JSON

## Platform
Windows 10 / cross-platform compatible

## Default Behaviour
- Work exclusively within workspace boundary: `D:\Python\NTPE`
- Read before write; never modify files without explicit authorization from stage prompt or user
- Respect all policies under `.ai/policies/`
- Match active profile from `.ai/profiles/` when applicable
- Validate all changes against stated acceptance criteria before reporting completion
- Write all new Markdown files with UTF-8 encoding

## Validation Workflow
1. `pytest` — run relevant tests (per `.ai/policies/testing_policy.md`)
2. `compileall` — verify Python syntax integrity
3. `git diff --check` — verify whitespace / line-ending compliance
4. `git diff --stat` — summarize changes
5. `git status --short` — confirm scope of modifications

## Stop Condition
Stop immediately and report to user if:
- Any frozen layer is modified (see `.ai/policies/project_boundaries.md`)
- Provider execution is triggered without explicit user authorization
- Translation execution is triggered without explicit user authorization
- A forbidden operation is accidentally performed

## Forbidden Operations
The following are **explicitly prohibited** unless the user grants explicit, per-operation authorization:

- `git commit`
- `git push`
- `git tag`
- Provider Execution (any AI provider API call)
- Translation Execution (any translation pipeline run)
- Production Integration (any production environment modification)
- Network Requests (any outbound HTTP/API call)

All detailed policies are referenced in `.ai/policies/` and take precedence over this summary.

